  "participant_contract": "Rolling final minus the separate frozen K0 path on all annotated reference positions. BLEU-1 is mean clipped unigram precision per subject-segment; word accuracy requires correct annotated positions. Three seed estimates and their arithmetic mean are shown; no participant confidence intervals are inferred.",
  "signal_time_contract": "Fixed common target events with both future arrivals available inside their replay segment; same targets at d=0,1,2 and across seeds. Signal availability = trace[i+d].input_window_end_seconds minus target onset[i]. Reported quantiles use each annotated target once per seed and are identical across seeds; seed copies are not pooled as independent targets. The initial signal already spans approximately 1 s after annotated target onset. Percentile spans describe targets, not uncertainty in accuracy.",
  "compute_contract": "Saved positive k0_decoder_seconds and k2_decoder_seconds per arrival, all evaluated steps, pooled across three seeds for the descriptive ECDF only. Hardware/implementation-specific offline replay costs; these are distinct from neural signal waiting. No end-to-end online latency claim and no sum of these distributions."
